chapter AFP

session UAF_Bug = OpSem +
  description \<open>
    Client: the paper's minimal 2-thread use-after-free example (uaf-bug.lit /
    uaf-bug-fixed.lit), instantiated against the Episodic OpSem stack (W9 / Phase 4,
    the fast end-to-end validation).

    Defines `prog_uaf_bug` / `prog_uaf_fixed` as Core-typed labelled `command` data
    and `Phi_uaf` / `Phi_uaf_fixed` as EventStruct `Phi` (edge-sets over `elabel`,
    adapted faithfully from the mordor-rendered generated digest).  The ONLY
    semantic difference between bug and fixed is the exit write's `mem_order`
    (relaxed vs `rel`) and hence the presence of the deref->exit ppo edge in Phi.

    States and proves (via the `opsem_client` locale): the UAF is REACHABLE in the
    buggy program (a `reachable` config has `Dealloc rC` enabled while T1's deref
    `Read rC` is still pending) and EXCLUDED in the fixed program (the release edge
    keeps the free out of the horizon until the deref has committed) -- matching the
    paper's `tab-fut-step-bug` / `-fix`.

    Imports OpSem (the non-loop `step` / `reachable` / `opsem_client` locale),
    session-qualified.
  \<close>
  options [timeout = 1200]
  sessions
    "Core"
    "MemSem"
    "EventStruct"
    "OpSem"
  theories
    UAF_Bug
